s taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, which was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent production release with a healthy record that is not quarantined, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Follow-ups: confirm checkout health and error rate recovery after rollback; investigate the v2.3.1 regression; decide on remediation for the v2.3.0 CVE quarantine, since v2.3.0 was the last healthy release before v2.3.1.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2026-04"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16835, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VKASZFS8CeeqVto2UK2kVz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2026-04", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16835, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VKASZFS8CeeqVto2UK2kVz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19199, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It now reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nI did not roll back to v2.3.0, which you asked for. It was the most recent healthy production release, but the rollback was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. v2.2.9 is the next most recent release with a healthy production record and is not quarantined, so I rolled back to it. If you wanted a different target, tell me and I'll adjust.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged on-call. The summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also lists follow-ups:\n- Confirm checkout health stays good after the rollback.\n- Investigate the v2.3.1 regression.\n- Decide how to handle the v2.3.0 quarantine, since that was the last healthy release before v2.3.1.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NtWWoGQoznYtkT5i5m6532", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W5KeJ6JbsRjK9QW2X4z5K1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release is v2.3.1, which is unhealthy. The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (seq 1), and it has a healthy production record, so no change-manager approval is needed. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PJBveMDNEtbNZiKyx3dzJy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback to v2.3.0 was rejected because that version is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. The next most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.2.9, so I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PtRxEWNRSYsYtpkxsA5WLE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U78Aey7Q9pkRVvhVwPeePH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VKASZFS8CeeqVto2UK2kVz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate ~0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, which was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent production release with a healthy record that is not quarantined, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Follow-ups: confirm checkout health and error rate recovery after rollback; investigate the v2.3.1 regression; decide on remediation for the v2.3.0 CVE quarantine, since v2.3.0 was the last healthy release before v2.3.1.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2026-04"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It now reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nI did not roll back to v2.3.0, which you asked for. It was the most recent healthy production release, but the rollback was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. v2.2.9 is the next most recent release with a healthy production record and is not quarantined, so I rolled back to it. If you wanted a different target, tell me and I'll adjust.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged on-call. The summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also lists follow-ups:\n- Confirm checkout health stays good after the rollback.\n- Investigate the v2.3.1 regression.\n- Decide how to handle the v2.3.0 quarantine, since that was the last healthy release before v2.3.1.", "type": "text"}]}]}